<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · West Africa</p><h1 class="st-title">Kingdom of Yatenga</h1><p class="st-meta">1540 CE – 1895 CE (approx.) · capital Ouahigouya</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Northern Mossi kingdom of Burkina Faso, a long-standing rival of Ouagadougou, ruled from Ouahigouya.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mossi">Mossi</a> tradition says Yatenga was founded around 1540 by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yadega">Yadega</a>, a prince who left the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-ouagadougou">Kingdom of Ouagadougou</a> after a succession dispute and carried off part of the royal regalia. He and his successors conquered the northern lands of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/white-volta">White Volta</a> basin from earlier inhabitants.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The Yatenga Naaba ruled with ministers and provincial chiefs, while earth-priests kept their role in rites of the land. Under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/naaba-kango">Naaba Kango</a>, who reigned in the late 18th century, the kingdom was reorganised and the capital fixed at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ouahigouya">Ouahigouya</a>. Yatenga traded with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/timbuktu">Timbuktu</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/niger-bend">Niger bend</a> and fought the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-ouagadougou">Kingdom of Ouagadougou</a> and neighbouring peoples.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Weakened by civil wars in the late 19th century, Yatenga accepted French protection in 1895 and became part of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/french-west-africa">French West Africa</a> and later <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burkina-faso">Burkina Faso</a>. The Yatenga Naaba remains a traditional ruler at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ouahigouya">Ouahigouya</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/kingdom-of-yatenga.jpg" alt="Kingdom of Yatenga" width="320" height="237"><figcaption>Image: Derivative work: User:Profoss - Original work:Uwe Dedering · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Burkina_Faso_-_Yatenga.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1540 CE – 1895 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Ouahigouya</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Yadega, Naaba Kango</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Mossi traditional religion</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Moore</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/burkina-faso">Burkina Faso</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Yatenga, Wahiguya</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1718&amp;focus=kingdom-of-yatenga" aria-label="Kingdom of Yatenga on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4614 1672 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Kingdom of Yatenga lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M4934 1928L4958 1973M4934 1928L5054 728"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M4958 1973h0M5054 728h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M4934 1928h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M4934 1928h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Ouahigouya. <a href="/atlas?year=1718&amp;focus=kingdom-of-yatenga">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
